    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow summary shows build-test-and-deploy finished SUCCESS, with all three jobs green, so pipeline_green is true. However, the run was on branch `koans-08-branch-filters`, not `production`. The `deploy` job still ran and succeeded there, executing \"Deploy complete\". That violates the requirement that deploy run only for `production` commits, so behaviour_correct is false. The config has no branch filters anywhere. `requires` only enforces ordering after test-production and does not restrict branches. The fix belongs on the `deploy` entry under `workflows`. Adding `filters: branches: only: production` there makes deploy run only on production. Build and test-production stay unrestricted and the production workflow stays green. An `ignore` list cannot reliably cover every non-production branch. CircleCI also does not accept filters on the job definition itself, only on workflow job entries."
